    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, the Austin Waves offense is constrained by a difficult matchup against Henderson, resulting in a conservative deployment of our available assets. **Kyle Tucker** (47.89) remains our strongest play despite being slotted into the 8-hole, as his elite profile helps him weather the suppression from a 3.13 xERA opponent. **Andy Pages** (42.21) earns the final UTIL spot primarily due to his utility in SB-scarce categories, though his production is strictly marginal against this caliber of starting pitching. We are managing our remaining capital carefully, prioritizing the protection of our daily game caps while acknowledging that our ceiling is depressed by the sheer strength of the opposing rotation.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench was **Brayan Rocchio** (34.02), who fell short of our 40-point \"Zebras\" efficiency floor. While **Brayan Rocchio** offers speed, his placement at the bottom of the order combined with a 3.30 xERA matchup against Rasmussen made him a statistical liability for today\u2019s specific scoring requirements. We are keeping **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** on the bench due to scheduled off-days or IL status, respectively; the absence of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill** is a significant blow to our total power output. With **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Luis Lara** also factoring into our broader roster management, we are playing for efficiency over volume today, explicitly avoiding any \"Below Floor\" starts that threaten our long-term cap health.",
